Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Fri Aug 14 06:22:22 2026 +1000

    Extend the nova_scheduler healthcheck timeout.
    
    Nova changed in 2026.1 how long their services take to gracefully
    shutdown.
    
      The default value of [DEFAULT]/graceful_shutdown_timeout has been
      changed from 60 to 180 seconds for all Nova services. [...]
      Operators using external system (e.g. k8s, systemd) to manage the
      Nova services should ensure that their service stop timeouts are
      set to at least graceful_shutdown_timeout to avoid forcefully
      killing service before Nova finish its graceful shutdown.
    
    Kolla-Ansible failed to update the period of time that ansible waits
    for Nova services to shut down. This causes both CI failures and
    failures for deployers when trying to manage some Nova containers.
    
    Prompt: Michael asked for assistance debugging why CI jobs were
    failing with nova-scheduler timeouts.
    
    Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context, high effort) <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context, high effort) <noreply@anthropic.com>
    
